From ffed416eab9cd9cef35e667bee5e3e97b32ce81a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:12:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] merge-manager-watcher: merge:watch's excluded layers default
 to smart-*

From the merge:watch upgrade (session session_01VQDpPg9URqDhr4fxtYeGmr):
check:reference-direction refused naming a higher layer in the default, so
the layers whose re-pins need the owner's consent now default to the
pattern smart-* (an entry ending in * matches a prefix); --exclude-layer
<name> or a config's excludedLayers replaces it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
---
 sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md b/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md
index 8a40090a..0267d89d 100644
--- a/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md
+++ b/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md
@@ -217,6 +217,10 @@ event, a merge request or a main run finishing may start a sweep early.
    Name the repositories with `--repo <owner/name>` (repeatable), `--repos
    a,b,c`, or `--config <file.json>` (`{"repos": [...], "staleHours": 2}`).
    `--stale-hours <n>` sets when a silent PR owner is flagged (default 2).
+   The layers whose re-pins need the owner's consent default to `smart-*`
+   (the WHO SMART upstream layers; an entry ending in `*` matches a
+   prefix). `--exclude-layer <name>` (repeatable) or a config's
+   `excludedLayers` replaces the default.
    Per repository it prints:
    - each PR's verdict, with a route flag: workflow changes go to a direct
      merge, a folio-assistant PR to the merge train, a pin on an excluded
